/-!
# Depth of local rings and modules: regular elements and depth attainment

First part of the proof of `exists_isRegular_map_length_eq_ringKrullDim` (Stacks 06LC), whose
overall argument is described in the section docstring below; the proof is completed in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.CohenMacaulay.RegularSequence.LocalRingMap`.

## Main results

* `exists_mem_maximalIdeal_isSMulRegular_map`: the prime-avoidance step, an element of `m_A` whose
  image in a Cohen–Macaulay local ring `B` of positive dimension is a nonzerodivisor.
* `depth_le_supportDim_self_quot`: `depth ≤ dim Supp` for `R / rR` (Stacks 00LK).
* `exists_isRegular_length_eq_depth_of_cohenMacaulay`,
  `exists_isRegular_length_eq_depth_of_depth_ne_top`: a regular sequence of length the depth.
* `depth_quotSMulTop_succ_le_depth`: the depth drops by at least one modulo a regular element.
* `depth_self_ne_top`: the depth of a Noetherian local ring is finite.
-/

/-!
# A regular sequence in `B` coming from a map of local rings

All rings are commutative. Let `A` and `B` be local rings, in the sense of a commutative
ring with a unique maximal ideal, and write `m_A` and `m_B` for their maximal ideals.

A map of local rings here means an arbitrary ring homomorphism `φ : A → B`; it is not
assumed local, so `φ(m_A) ⊆ m_B` is not a hypothesis, and the equation
`m_B = √(φ(m_A) B)` does the work instead.

The main result: if `B` is Noetherian and Cohen-Macaulay and `m_B = √(φ(m_A) B)`, then
there is a list `f` of elements of `A` of length `dim B` such that the images
`φ(f₁), …, φ(f_{dim B})` form a regular sequence in `B` as a module over itself.

## Notions used

Being a Cohen-Macaulay local ring is `IsCohenMacaulayLocalRing B`, definitionally
`IsCohenMacaulayModule B B`, taking the instances `[IsNoetherianRing B]` and
`[IsLocalRing B]`; it appears below as an ordinary hypothesis. The radical of an ideal is
`Ideal.radical I = {x | ∃ n, x ^ n ∈ I}`, and the extension `φ(m_A) B` of an ideal along
`φ` is `Ideal.map φ m_A`, the ideal of `B` generated by the image, so the radical
hypothesis reads
`IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B = (Ideal.map φ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)).radical`.

The Krull dimension is `ringKrullDim B : WithBot ℕ∞`, a finite natural number for a nonzero
Noetherian local ring, and lengths are compared inside `WithBot ℕ∞` as
`(f.length : WithBot ℕ∞) = ringKrullDim B`. Finally
`RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular B (f.map φ)`, for `f : List A`, says that the images
`φ(f₁), …, φ(f_c)` form a regular sequence in `B` over itself; this includes the properness
condition `(φ(f₁), …, φ(f_c)) ≠ B`, which is automatic here since all `φ(fᵢ)` lie in `m_B`.

## Shape of the argument

The whole argument is an induction on `d = dim B`, carried by the engine lemma
`exists_list_isRegular_map_of_ringKrullDim_eq`, inside which the ring `B` is universally
quantified so that the induction hypothesis can be applied to the quotient `B ⧸ (φ f₀)`, a
different ring of dimension `d - 1`.

The substantive Cohen-Macaulay input is isolated as `exists_mem_maximalIdeal_isSMulRegular_map`:
when `dim B = n + 1`, prime avoidance together with the absence of embedded primes in a
Cohen-Macaulay ring produces `f₀ ∈ m_A` whose image `φ f₀` is a nonzerodivisor, along with
the hypotheses that let the induction continue on the quotient. The rest is length
bookkeeping, `isRegular_cons_iff`, and the dimension drop
`ringKrullDim_le_ringKrullDim_quotSMulTop_succ`.
-/

@[expose] public section

/-- **CM no-embedded-primes / prime-avoidance step (Stacks 02JN + 00DS).**
Engine of the inductive step.  Suppose `B` is a Noetherian Cohen–Macaulay local
ring of dimension `n + 1`, `φ : A →+* B` a ring hom with
`m_B = sqrt(φ(m_A) B)`.  Then there is an element `f₀ ∈ m_A` whose image
`φ f₀ ∈ m_B` is a non-zero-divisor on `B` (equivalently `IsSMulRegular B (φ f₀)`).

INFORMAL PROOF.
* Because `B` is Noetherian it has finitely many minimal primes
  `q₁, …, q_r` (`minimalPrimes.finite_of_isNoetherianRing`, Stacks 00FR).
* Because `B` is Cohen–Macaulay it has no embedded associated primes: every
  associated prime is minimal (unmixedness, Stacks 02JN-flavoured).  Hence the
  set of zero-divisors of `B` is exactly `⋃ qᵢ`, so an element of `B` is a
  non-zero-divisor iff it lies in no minimal prime `qᵢ`.
* The radical hypothesis forces, for each `i`, `m_A ⊄ φ⁻¹(qᵢ)`.  Indeed, if
  `m_A ⊆ φ⁻¹(qᵢ)` then `φ(m_A) ⊆ qᵢ`, so `Ideal.map φ m_A ⊆ qᵢ`, hence
  `m_B = sqrt(φ(m_A)B) ⊆ sqrt(qᵢ) = qᵢ` (a prime equals its own radical).  But
  `dim B = n + 1 ≥ 1` makes `m_B` strictly larger than every minimal prime, a
  contradiction.  (`φ⁻¹(qᵢ) = Ideal.comap φ qᵢ` is prime as a comap of a prime.)
* Prime avoidance (`Ideal.subset_union_prime`, Stacks 00DS) applied to the ideal
  `m_A` and the primes `φ⁻¹(q₁), …, φ⁻¹(q_r)`: since `m_A ⊄ φ⁻¹(qᵢ)` for all `i`,
  `m_A` is not contained in their union, so there is `f₀ ∈ m_A` with
  `f₀ ∉ φ⁻¹(qᵢ)`, i.e. `φ f₀ ∉ qᵢ`, for every `i`.  As `φ f₀` avoids all minimal
  primes it is a non-zero-divisor, i.e. `IsSMulRegular B (φ f₀)`; and `f₀ ∈ m_A`
  gives `φ f₀ ∈ Ideal.map φ m_A ⊆ m_B`. -/
theorem exists_mem_maximalIdeal_isSMulRegular_map {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
  [IsLocalRing A]
    [IsLocalRing B] [IsNoetherianRing B] (hCM : IsCohenMacaulayLocalRing B) (φ : A →+* B)
    (h : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B = (Ideal.map φ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)).radical) (n : ℕ)
    (hdim : ringKrullDim B = ((n + 1 : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    ∃ f₀ : A,
      f₀ ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ∧
        φ f₀ ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B ∧ IsSMulRegular B (φ f₀) := by
  classical
  -- STEP 1: From the Cohen–Macaulay hypothesis and `dim B = n+1`, the depth of
  -- `B` along its maximal ideal is exactly `n+1` (as `ℕ∞`).
  --   CM : ↑(depth m_B B) = krullDim (support B B) = supportDim B B
  --      = ringKrullDim B = n+1.
  have hdepth : Module.depthSup B (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B) B = ((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℕ∞) := by
    have hCM' := hCM
    unfold IsCohenMacaulayLocalRing IsCohenMacaulayModule at hCM'
    have hsd : Module.supportDim B B = ringKrullDim B := Module.supportDim_self_eq_ringKrullDim B
    rw [Module.supportDim] at hsd
    rw [hsd, hdim] at hCM'
    have :
      ((Module.depthSup B (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B) B : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) =
        (((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
      exact_mod_cast hCM'
    exact_mod_cast this
  -- STEP 2: Since `depth ≥ 1`, there is a regular sequence in `m_B` of positive
  -- length, whose head is a non-zero-divisor `r ∈ m_B`.
  have hexNZD : ∃ r : B, r ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B ∧ IsSMulRegular B r := by
    rw [Module.depthSup] at hdepth
    set S :=
      {m : ℕ∞ |
        ∃ rs : List B,
          ↑rs.length = m ∧
            (∀ r ∈ rs, r ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B) ∧ RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular B rs} with
      hS
    have h1 : (1 : ℕ∞) ≤ sSup S := by
      rw [hdepth]; exact_mod_cast Nat.le_add_left 1 n
    have hexk : ∃ k ∈ S, (1 : ℕ∞) ≤ k := by
      by_contra hc
      push Not at hc
      have hub : ∀ k ∈ S, k ≤ 0 := by
        intro k hk
        have hlt := hc k hk
        have hk0 : k = 0 := by
          rcases eq_or_ne k 0 with h0 | h0
          · exact h0
          · exact
              absurd hlt
                (by
                  have : (1 : ℕ∞) ≤ k := Order.one_le_iff_ne_zero.mpr h0
                  simp [not_lt.mpr this])
        simp [hk0]
      have hle0 : sSup S ≤ 0 := sSup_le hub
      exact absurd (le_trans h1 hle0) (by norm_num)
    obtain ⟨k, hkS, hk1⟩ := hexk
    obtain ⟨rs, hlen, hmem, hreg⟩ := hkS
    have hne : rs ≠ [] := by
      rintro rfl
      simp only [List.length_nil] at hlen
      rw [← hlen] at hk1
      exact absurd hk1 (by norm_num)
    obtain ⟨r, rest, rfl⟩ := List.exists_cons_of_ne_nil hne
    refine ⟨r, hmem r (List.mem_cons_self), ?_⟩
    rw [RingTheory.Sequence.isRegular_cons_iff] at hreg
    exact hreg.left
  obtain ⟨r, hrmem, hrreg⟩ := hexNZD
  -- STEP 3: `m_B` is not an associated prime of `B`: it contains the NZD `r`,
  -- yet every element of an associated prime is a zero-divisor.
  have hmBnot : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B ∉ associatedPrimes B B := by
    intro hmem
    have hbu := biUnion_associatedPrimes_eq_compl_nonZeroDivisors B
    have hrZD : r ∈ (↑(nonZeroDivisors B) : Set B)ᶜ := by
      rw [← hbu]; simp only [Set.mem_iUnion]
      exact ⟨IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B, hmem, hrmem⟩
    have hrNZD : r ∈ nonZeroDivisors B := by
      rw [mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff]
      refine ⟨fun x hx => ?_, fun x hx => ?_⟩
      · apply hrreg; simp only [smul_eq_mul, mul_zero, hx]
      · apply hrreg; simp only [smul_eq_mul, mul_zero]; rw [mul_comm]; exact hx
    exact hrZD hrNZD
  -- STEP 4: For each associated prime `p`, `m_A ⊄ φ⁻¹(p)`.  Otherwise
  -- `map φ m_A ≤ p`, so `m_B = sqrt(map φ m_A) ≤ p`, forcing `p = m_B`
  -- (maximality), contradicting STEP 3.
  have havoid : ∀ p ∈ associatedPrimes B B, ¬(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ≤ Ideal.comap φ p) := by
    intro p hp hle
    have hmap : Ideal.map φ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) ≤ p := by
      rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]; exact hle
    have hpprime : p.IsPrime := hp.isPrime
    have hrad : (Ideal.map φ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)).radical ≤ p := by
      rw [← hpprime.radical]; exact Ideal.radical_mono hmap
    have hmBle : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B ≤ p := by
      rw [h]; exact hrad
    have hpne : p ≠ ⊤ := hpprime.ne_top
    have hpeq : p = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B :=
      le_antisymm (IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal hpne) hmBle
    rw [hpeq] at hp
    exact hmBnot hp
  -- STEP 5: Prime avoidance (00DS) for `m_A` against the finitely many primes
  -- `φ⁻¹(p)`, `p ∈ Ass(B)`: produces `f₀ ∈ m_A` with `φ f₀ ∉ p` for all `p`.
  have hf0 :
    ∃ f₀ : A, f₀ ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ∧ (∀ p ∈ associatedPrimes B B, φ f₀ ∉ p) := by
    have hfin : (associatedPrimes B B).Finite := associatedPrimes.finite B B
    set sF : Finset (Ideal B) := hfin.toFinset with hsF
    set g : Ideal B → Ideal A := fun p => Ideal.comap φ p with hg
    obtain ⟨p0, hp0⟩ := associatedPrimes.nonempty B B
    have hprime : ∀ q ∈ sF, q ≠ p0 → q ≠ p0 → (g q).IsPrime := by
      intro q hq _ _
      have hqmem : q ∈ associatedPrimes B B := by
        rw [hsF] at hq; exact hfin.mem_toFinset.mp hq
      have : q.IsPrime := hqmem.isPrime
      exact Ideal.comap_isPrime φ q
    have hiff :=
      Ideal.subset_union_prime (s := sF) (f := g) p0 p0 hprime (I := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    have hnotex : ¬(∃ q ∈ sF, IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ≤ g q) := by
      push Not
      intro q hq
      have hqmem : q ∈ associatedPrimes B B := by
        rw [hsF] at hq; exact hfin.mem_toFinset.mp hq
      exact havoid q hqmem
    have hnotsub : ¬((↑(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) : Set A) ⊆ ⋃ q ∈ sF, ↑(g q)) := fun hc =>
      hnotex (hiff.mp hc)
    rw [Set.not_subset] at hnotsub
    obtain ⟨f₀, hf0mem, hf0not⟩ := hnotsub
    refine ⟨f₀, hf0mem, ?_⟩
    intro p hp hcontra
    apply hf0not
    simp only [Set.mem_iUnion]
    exact
      ⟨p, by
        rw [hsF]; exact hfin.mem_toFinset.mpr hp, by
        rw [hg]; exact Ideal.mem_comap.mpr hcontra⟩
  -- STEP 6: Assemble.  `φ f₀ ∈ m_B` (image of `m_A` lands in its radical
  -- `= m_B`); and avoiding all associated primes makes `φ f₀` a NZD, hence
  -- `IsSMulRegular B (φ f₀)`.
  obtain ⟨f₀, hf0mem, hf0avoid⟩ := hf0
  refine ⟨f₀, hf0mem, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [h]; exact Ideal.le_radical (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem φ hf0mem)
  · have hbu := biUnion_associatedPrimes_eq_compl_nonZeroDivisors B
    have hNZD : φ f₀ ∈ nonZeroDivisors B := by
      by_contra hc
      have hmemc : φ f₀ ∈ (↑(nonZeroDivisors B) : Set B)ᶜ := hc
      rw [← hbu] at hmemc
      simp only [Set.mem_iUnion] at hmemc
      obtain ⟨p, hp, hmem⟩ := hmemc
      exact hf0avoid p hp hmem
    rw [mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff] at hNZD
    intro x y hxy
    simp only [smul_eq_mul] at hxy
    have hz : φ f₀ * (x - y) = 0 := by rw [mul_sub, hxy, sub_self]
    exact sub_eq_zero.mp (hNZD.left (x - y) hz)

/-! ### Cohen-Macaulayness descends to a quotient by a regular element

The statement `cohenMacaulay_quotient_span_singleton_of_isSMulRegular` is assembled by
antisymmetry from three pieces: `depth_le_supportDim_self_quot`,
`supportDim_le_depth_quotSMulTop_of_cohenMacaulay`, and the characterization
`cohenMacaulay_quot_iff_depth_eq_supportDim`.
-/

/-- A module of support dimension `e` has depth at most `e`. -/
private theorem depthSup_le_of_supportDim_eq {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M] (e : ℕ∞)
    (he : Module.supportDim R M = e) : Module.depthSup R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) M ≤ e := by
  rw [Module.depthSup]
  refine sSup_le ?_
  rintro n ⟨rs, rfl, -, hreg⟩
  have heq := Module.supportDim_add_length_eq_supportDim_of_isRegular rs hreg
  rw [he] at heq
  induction hb : Module.supportDim R (M ⧸ Ideal.ofList rs • (⊤ : Submodule R M)) using
    WithBot.recBotCoe with
  | bot => simp [hb] at heq
  | coe v =>
    rw [hb] at heq
    norm_cast at heq
    exact heq ▸ le_add_self

/-- A module of finite support dimension has finite depth. -/
private theorem depthSup_ne_top_of_supportDim_eq {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M] (e : ℕ)
    (he : Module.supportDim R M = e) : Module.depthSup R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) M ≠ ⊤ :=
  ne_top_of_le_ne_top (ENat.natCast_ne_top e) (depthSup_le_of_supportDim_eq e (by rw [he]; rfl))

/-- The Krull dimension of a Noetherian local ring is a natural number. -/
private theorem exists_natCast_eq_ringKrullDim (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] : ∃ d : ℕ, ringKrullDim R = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have hne_top : ringKrullDim R ≠ ⊤ := ringKrullDim_ne_top
  have hnonneg : 0 ≤ ringKrullDim R := ringKrullDim_nonneg_of_nontrivial
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := WithBot.ne_bot_iff_exists.mp (ne_bot_of_le_ne_bot WithBot.zero_ne_bot hnonneg)
  lift y to ℕ using fun h => hne_top (by rw [← hy, h]; rfl) with n
  exact ⟨n, hy.symm⟩

/-- **Depth ≤ supportDim for `QuotSMulTop r R`** (general inequality, Stacks 00LK).
For a Noetherian local ring `R` and the finite module `N = QuotSMulTop r R`, the
depth of `N` along `m_R` is at most its support dimension.

*Proof.*  No Rees theorem is needed.  For any
`N`-regular sequence `xs ⊆ m_R` of length `k`, the dimension-drop lemma
`Module.supportDim_add_length_eq_supportDim_of_isRegular xs` gives
`supportDim R (N ⧸ ofList xs • ⊤) + k = supportDim R N`; since supportDim of a
(possibly zero) module is `≥ ⊥` and is `≥ 0` when nonzero, `k ≤ supportDim R N`.
As `Module.depthSup R m_R N = sSup {k | ∃ such xs}`, taking the sSup gives
`depth ≤ supportDim`.  Cite: `Module.supportDim_add_length_eq_supportDim_of_isRegular`,
`Module.depthSup` (its `sSup` definition), `sSup_le`. -/
theorem depth_le_supportDim_self_quot {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    {r : R} (hrm : r ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) :
    (↑(Module.depthSup R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) (QuotSMulTop r R)) : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤
      Module.supportDim R (QuotSMulTop r R) := by
  -- `r ∈ m_R` rules out the edge case `N = 0`, where `depth = 0 > ⊥ = supportDim`.
  -- Bound each regular-sequence length by supportDim via
  -- `Module.supportDim_add_length_eq_supportDim_of_isRegular`, then take the sSup.
  set N := QuotSMulTop r R with hN
  have : Nontrivial N := nontrivial_quotSMulTop_of_mem_maximalIdeal R hrm
  -- `supportDim R N ≠ ⊥` because `N` is nonzero.
  have hbot : Module.supportDim R N ≠ ⊥ := by
    change Order.krullDim ↑(Module.support R N) ≠ ⊥
    rw [Ne, Order.krullDim_eq_bot_iff, not_isEmpty_iff]
    have hne : Module.support R N ≠ ∅ := by
      rw [Ne, Module.support_eq_empty_iff]
      exact not_subsingleton N
    rw [← Set.nonempty_iff_ne_empty] at hne
    exact hne.to_subtype
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := WithBot.ne_bot_iff_exists.mp hbot
  -- `he : ↑e = supportDim R N`.  Reduce the goal to `depth ≤ e` in `ℕ∞`.
  rw [← he, WithBot.coe_le_coe]
  exact depthSup_le_of_supportDim_eq e he.symm

/- **supportDim ≤ depth for `QuotSMulTop r R` from Cohen–Macaulayness** (Stacks 00LF).
For a Noetherian Cohen–Macaulay local ring `R` and a regular element `r ∈ m_R`,
there is a regular sequence on `N = QuotSMulTop r R` lying in `m_R` whose length
is at least `supportDim R N`
(`exists_isRegular_quotSMulTop_length_ge_supportDim_of_cohenMacaulay`), whence
`supportDim R N ≤ depth R m_R N` (`supportDim_le_depth_quotSMulTop_of_cohenMacaulay`).

INFORMAL PROOF (Stacks 00LK / 00N6).  Because `R` is CM of dimension
`d = ringKrullDim R = supportDim R R = depth R m_R R`, the depth `sSup` is attained
by a *maximal* `R`-regular sequence in `m_R` of length exactly `d`
(the depth-index set `{k | ∃ regular seq in m_R of length k}` is a nonempty —
`0` via `IsRegular.nil` — subset of the finite chain `{0,…,d}` bounded above by
`d` via `Module.supportDim_add_length_eq_supportDim_of_isRegular`, so its `sSup`
is its maximum and lies in the set).  Every regular element `r ∈ m_R` extends to
such a maximal regular sequence with `r` as its head (Stacks 00LK: regular
sequences in `m_R` extend to maximal ones, all of common length `depth`; the
head-placement uses prime avoidance over `associatedPrimes`).  Dropping `r` via
`RingTheory.Sequence.isRegular_cons_iff` leaves an `N`-regular sequence `rs` in
`m_R` of length `d - 1`; by `Module.supportDim_quotSMulTop_succ_eq_supportDim`,
`supportDim R N + 1 = supportDim R R = d`, so `supportDim R N = d - 1 = ↑rs.length`.

The argument goes through depth: positive support dimension alone does not give a regular
element of `m_R` on a module (for `R = PowerSeries ℚ` and `M = (R⧸m) × R`, the embedded
associated prime `m_R` coexists with support of dimension one). -/

/-- Depth attainment: a finite depth is the length of a regular sequence in `m_R`. -/
private theorem exists_isRegular_length_eq_depth_aux {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    [Nontrivial M]
    (hfin : Module.depthSup R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) M ≠ ⊤) :
    ∃ ms : List R,
      (∀ x ∈ ms, x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) ∧
        RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular M ms ∧
        ((ms.length : ℕ∞) = Module.depthSup R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) M) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := ENat.ne_top_iff_exists.mp hfin
  set m := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R with hm
  set S :=
    {n : ℕ∞ |
      ∃ rs : List R, ↑rs.length = n ∧ (∀ r ∈ rs, r ∈ m) ∧ RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular M rs} with
    hS
  have hdepthS : Module.depthSup R m M = sSup S := by rw [Module.depthSup]
  have h0S : (0 : ℕ∞) ∈ S := by
    refine ⟨[], by simp, by simp, RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular.nil R M⟩
  have hSne : S.Nonempty := ⟨0, h0S⟩
  -- bound: every x ∈ S ≤ ↑d, since x ≤ sSup S = depth = ↑d
  have hbound : ∀ x ∈ S, x ≤ (d : ℕ∞) := by
    intro x hx
    have hxle : x ≤ sSup S := le_sSup hx
    rw [← hdepthS, ← hd] at hxle
    exact hxle
  -- attainment: sSup S ∈ S
  have hattain : sSup S ∈ S := by
    set T : Set ℕ := {k : ℕ | (k : ℕ∞) ∈ S} with hT
    have hTne : T.Nonempty :=
      ⟨0, by
        rw [hT, Set.mem_ofPred_eq, Nat.cast_zero]; exact h0S⟩
    have hTbdd : BddAbove T :=
      ⟨d, fun k hk => by
        have : (k : ℕ∞) ≤ (d : ℕ∞) := hbound _ hk
        exact_mod_cast this⟩
    have hmem := Nat.sSup_mem hTne hTbdd
    have hkey : sSup S = ((sSup T : ℕ) : ℕ∞) := by
      apply le_antisymm
      · apply sSup_le
        intro x hx
        have hxd : x ≤ (d : ℕ∞) := hbound x hx
        have hxne : x ≠ ⊤ := by
          rintro rfl; simp only [top_le_iff] at hxd; exact absurd hxd (by simp)
        lift x to ℕ using hxne with k
        have hkT : k ∈ T := hx
        have : k ≤ sSup T := le_csSup hTbdd hkT
        exact_mod_cast this
      · exact le_sSup hmem
    rw [hkey]; exact hmem
  obtain ⟨ms, hlen, hmem, hreg⟩ := hattain
  refine ⟨ms, hmem, hreg, ?_⟩
  rw [hlen, ← hdepthS]

/-- **Depth attainment.**  In a Noetherian Cohen–Macaulay local ring `R`,
the depth `sSup` is attained: there is an `R`-regular sequence in `m_R` of length
exactly `ringKrullDim R`.

INFORMAL PROOF.  Let `d = ringKrullDim R`
and `S = {n : ℕ∞ | ∃ rs, ↑rs.length = n ∧ (∀ x ∈ rs, x ∈ m_R) ∧ IsRegular R rs}`
be the depth index set, so `Module.depthSup R m_R R = sSup S`.
* `0 ∈ S` via `RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular.nil` (`R` nontrivial, local).
* `S` is bounded above by `d`: for `rs ∈ S`,
  `Module.supportDim_add_length_eq_supportDim_of_isRegular` +
  `Module.supportDim_self_eq_ringKrullDim` give `↑rs.length ≤ d`.
* CM unfolds to `depth R m_R R = supportDim R R = d`, so `sSup S = d`.
A nonempty subset of `ℕ∞` bounded above by the finite `d` attains its `sSup`
(`Nat.sSup_mem` through the order-iso on the finite part of `ℕ∞`), so `d ∈ S`:
there is an honest regular sequence of length `d`.  CM enters only to evaluate
`depth = d`. -/
@[ega "0 16.5.9" "special case"]
theorem exists_isRegular_length_eq_depth_of_cohenMacaulay {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R] (hCM : IsCohenMacaulayLocalRing R) :
    ∃ ss : List R,
      (∀ x ∈ ss, x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) ∧
        RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R ss ∧
        ((ss.length : ℕ∞) = Module.depthSup R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R) := by
  classical
  have hCM' := hCM
  unfold IsCohenMacaulayLocalRing IsCohenMacaulayModule at hCM'
  have hsd : Module.supportDim R R = ringKrullDim R := Module.supportDim_self_eq_ringKrullDim R
  rw [Module.supportDim] at hsd
  rw [hsd] at hCM'
  refine exists_isRegular_length_eq_depth_aux fun htop => ringKrullDim_ne_top (R := R) ?_
  rw [htop] at hCM'
  rw [← hCM']; rfl

/-- **Depth attainment for a finite module with finite depth** (general; no CM).
If `Module.depthSup R m_R M ≠ ⊤`, the depth `sSup` over the regular-sequence index set
is attained: there is an `M`-regular sequence in `m_R` of length exactly
`Module.depthSup R m_R M`.

INFORMAL PROOF.  `Module.depthSup R m_R M = sSup S` where `S = {n : ℕ∞ | ∃ rs,
↑rs.length = n ∧ entries ∈ m_R ∧ IsRegular M rs}`.  `0 ∈ S` via `IsRegular.nil`
(needs `[Nontrivial M]`).  Since `sSup S = depth ≠ ⊤`, every element of `S` is `≤
sSup S < ⊤`, so `S` transports to a nonempty subset `T ⊆ ℕ` bounded above by the
finite value of `sSup S`; `Nat.sSup_mem` gives `sSup T ∈ T`, and `sSup S = ↑(sSup T)`
by antisymmetry, so `sSup S ∈ S`.  This is the attainment argument of
`exists_isRegular_length_eq_depth_of_cohenMacaulay`, with the finiteness coming from the
hypothesis `hfin` instead of CM. -/
@[ega "0 16.5.9" "special case"]
theorem exists_isRegular_length_eq_depth_of_depth_ne_top {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    [Module.Finite R M] [Nontrivial M]
    (hfin : Module.depthSup R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) M ≠ ⊤) :
    ∃ ms : List R,
      (∀ x ∈ ms, x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) ∧
        RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular M ms ∧
        ((ms.length : ℕ∞) = Module.depthSup R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) M) := by
  exact exists_isRegular_length_eq_depth_aux hfin

-- needed: `depth_quotSMulTop_succ_le_depth`'s `decide` on `¬0 ≤ none` in `ℕ∞` only reduces
-- its `Decidable` instance at `default` transparency
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false in
/-- **Depth drops by at least one modulo a regular element.**  For an `R`-regular element
`r ∈ m_R`, the depth of `N = QuotSMulTop r R` drops by at least one:
`depth R m_R N + 1 ≤ depth R m_R R`.

INFORMAL PROOF.  Let `SN`, `SR`
be the depth index sets for `N` and `R`.  For any `N`-regular `us` in `m_R` of
length `k`, `RingTheory.Sequence.isRegular_cons_iff` with `⟨hr, hus⟩` makes `r :: us`
an `R`-regular sequence in `m_R` of length `k + 1`; hence `k + 1 ∈ SR` whenever
`k ∈ SN` (transported to ℕ∞).  Since `depth N` is finite and attained
(`exists_isRegular_length_eq_depth_of_depth_ne_top`), this gives `sSup SN + 1 ≤ sSup SR`,
i.e. `depth N + 1 ≤ depth R`. -/
@[ega "0 16.4.6" "(ii)", sga "2 III 2.5" "partial", sga "2 XII 3.4" "partial"]
theorem depth_quotSMulTop_succ_le_depth {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] {r : R} (hr : IsSMulRegular R r) (hrm : r ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) :
    Module.depthSup R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) (QuotSMulTop r R) + 1 ≤
      Module.depthSup R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R := by
  classical
  set m := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R with hm
  set N := QuotSMulTop r R with hN
  -- `N` is nontrivial (`r ∈ m_R` is a non-unit, so `r • ⊤ ≠ ⊤`).
  have hNnt : Nontrivial N := nontrivial_quotSMulTop_of_mem_maximalIdeal R hrm
  -- `depth N ≠ ⊤`: regular-seq lengths on `N` are bounded by `supportDim N`, which is
  -- finite since `supportDim N + 1 = supportDim R = ringKrullDim R < ⊤`.
  have hNfin : Module.depthSup R m N ≠ ⊤ := by
    -- ringKrullDim R = ↑d (finite).
    obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := exists_natCast_eq_ringKrullDim R
    -- supportDim N + 1 = supportDim R = ringKrullDim R = ↑d.
    have hsuppN : Module.supportDim R N + 1 = Module.supportDim R R := by
      have := Module.supportDim_quotSMulTop_succ_eq_supportDim (R := R) (M := R) hr hrm
      simpa [hN] using this
    have hself : Module.supportDim R R = ringKrullDim R := Module.supportDim_self_eq_ringKrullDim R
    -- supportDim N = ↑e for some e : ℕ (e = d - 1).  Bound regular-seq lengths by e.
    obtain ⟨e, he⟩ : ∃ e : ℕ, Module.supportDim R N = (e : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
      have hsumeq : Module.supportDim R N + 1 = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) := by rw [hsuppN, hself, hd]
      have hne_bot : Module.supportDim R N ≠ ⊥ := by
        intro hxb
        rw [hxb, WithBot.bot_add] at hsumeq
        exact absurd hsumeq (by simp)
      have hne_top : Module.supportDim R N ≠ (⊤ : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
        intro hxt
        rw [hxt, show (⊤ : WithBot ℕ∞) + 1 = ⊤ from rfl] at hsumeq
        have : ((d : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) ≠ ⊤ := by exact_mod_cast (ENat.natCast_ne_top d)
        exact this hsumeq.symm
      obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := WithBot.ne_bot_iff_exists.mp hne_bot
      have hyt : y ≠ ⊤ := by
        rintro rfl; rw [← hy] at hne_top; simp at hne_top
      lift y to ℕ using hyt with e
      exact ⟨e, hy.symm⟩
    exact depthSup_ne_top_of_supportDim_eq e he
  -- Depth attainment for `N`: an `N`-regular `us` in `m` of length `depth N`.
  obtain ⟨us, husmem, husreg, huslen⟩ :=
    exists_isRegular_length_eq_depth_of_depth_ne_top (M := N) hNfin
  -- `r :: us` is `R`-regular in `m` of length `depth N + 1`, so it sits in `S_R`.
  set SR :=
    {n : ℕ∞ |
      ∃ rs : List R, ↑rs.length = n ∧ (∀ r ∈ rs, r ∈ m) ∧ RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R rs} with
    hSR
  have hmemSR : (Module.depthSup R m N + 1) ∈ SR := by
    refine ⟨r :: us, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [List.length_cons, Nat.cast_add, Nat.cast_one, huslen]
    · intro x hx
      rcases List.mem_cons.mp hx with h | h
      · rw [h]; exact hrm
      · exact husmem x h
    · rw [RingTheory.Sequence.isRegular_cons_iff]
      exact ⟨hr, husreg⟩
  have hdepthSR : Module.depthSup R m R = sSup SR := by rw [Module.depthSup]
  rw [hdepthSR]
  exact le_sSup hmemSR

-- needed: `depth_self_ne_top`'s `decide` on `¬0 ≤ none` in `ℕ∞` only reduces its
-- `Decidable` instance at `default` transparency
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false in
/-- **`depth R m_R R` is finite** for a Noetherian local ring `R`.
Regular-sequence lengths in `m_R` are bounded by `supportDim R R = ringKrullDim R`,
which is finite (`ringKrullDim_ne_top`), so the depth `sSup` is `≠ ⊤`.  No
Cohen–Macaulay hypothesis is needed. -/
@[ega "0 16.4.5" "prof(A) < +∞ for M = A", sga "2 III 2.7" "special case"]
theorem depth_self_ne_top {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R] :
    Module.depthSup R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R ≠ ⊤ := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := exists_natCast_eq_ringKrullDim R
  exact depthSup_ne_top_of_supportDim_eq d (by rw [Module.supportDim_self_eq_ringKrullDim, hd])

end
